<title>NEW ZEALAND: TABLE-Telecom Q1 profit NZ$188 mln.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Telecom Q1 profit NZ$188 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				188.0 vs 177.1</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 10.3 vs 9.4</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				 10.5 vs 9.5</p>
<p>    Turnover				   800.6 vs 730.7</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    280.4 vs 279.6</p>
<p>    Tax					   89.9 vs 91.2</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	  1.89 vs 1.89</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date Sept 17</p>
<p>Reg date Sept  5  </p>
<p>Note - Telecom Corp of New Zealand is a telephone utility owned 24.8 percent by Ameritech Corp and 24.8 percent by Bell Atlantic Corp. Analysts had forecast a net profit of about NZ$190 million.</p>
<p>Balance sheet (in billions unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current assets			    0.82 vs 0.84</p>
<p>    Total assets				4.65 vs 4.58</p>
<p>    Current liabilities		     1.55 vs 1.11</p>
<p>    Total liabilities			 2.96 vs 2.44</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		    1.41 vs 2.14</p>
<p>Cashflow from operating activities  0.42 vs 0.38  </p>
<p>Cashflow from investing activities(0.22) vs (0.23)</p>
